{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (PATIENT): Ag, sorry we're late. The robot by the garage was out and the traffic was hectic.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right. Sit. What is it.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (PATIENT): I nearly turned around. I'm tired and this whole morning has been a waste.",
  "[SEG0004] person_3 (CAREGIVER): She was up before five. I told her we are not missing the appointment.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (PATIENT): Ja well I've got a class to teach before the bell, so can we move.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (DOCTOR): The reason.",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (PATIENT): It's, umm, I don't want a whole fuss about—",
  "[SEG0008] person_3 (CAREGIVER): Tell him about the—",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (PATIENT): I'm telling him. I found a lump. Left breast. In the shower.",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (DOCTOR): How long.",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (PATIENT): Err. My head's not working this morning.",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (CAREGIVER): She only showed me after she kept going back to check.",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (PATIENT): Two weeks. It doesn't hurt.",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (DOCTOR): The lump, painful.",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (DOCTOR): Nipple discharge.",
  "[SEG0017] person_1 (PATIENT): No. Nothing comes out.",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (DOCTOR): Bigger since you found it.",
  "[SEG0019] person_1 (PATIENT): Same. Hard, like a, well, like a marble, upper part towards the arm.",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (DOCTOR): Breast cancer in the family.",
  "[SEG0021] person_1 (PATIENT): Umm.",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (CAREGIVER): In the car her sister was pushing biotin, for her own hair. Some vitamin. Nothing to do with this.",
  "[SEG0023] person_1 (PATIENT): Ag, stop with the biotin. My mother. Breast cancer. She was 55.",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (DOCTOR): Anyone else.",
  "[SEG0025] person_1 (PATIENT): No. Just her. She's alright now, hey, that was years ago.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (DOCTOR): Tablets you take.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (PATIENT): Microval, one a day. Vitamin D, a thousand units, meant to be every day.",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (DOCTOR): And is it every day.",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (PATIENT): The pill, ja. The vitamin D I forget half the time.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any drug reaction. Ever.",
  "[SEG0031] person_1 (PATIENT): No, never. I have taken penicillin and everything. Amoxacillin for a tooth years back, no problem.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (DOCTOR): Do you smoke.",
  "[SEG0033] person_1 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (DOCTOR): Alcohol.",
  "[SEG0035] person_1 (PATIENT): A glass of wine at the weekend. That's all. Can we just get on with it.",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (DOCTOR): Lie back. Examining both sides.",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (DOCTOR): Left upper outer quadrant, a firm mobile lump, about 2 centimetres. Skin normal, no tethering, nipple not pulled in. Right breast clear. No nodes in the axilla.",
  "[SEG0038] person_1 (PATIENT): Two centimetres. Fantastic.",
  "[SEG0039] person_2 (DOCTOR): I'm referring you urgently to the breast clinic. You'll be seen within two weeks. They'll do a mammogram and an ultrasound.",
  "[SEG0040] person_1 (PATIENT): So you think it's cancer.",
  "[SEG0041] person_2 (DOCTOR): I can't tell you that. It may be a cyst, it may be something else. Don't take the biotin.",
  "[SEG0042] person_3 (CAREGIVER): It's her sister's bottle, I said so in the car.",
  "[SEG0043] person_2 (DOCTOR): If the lump grows quickly, or there's discharge, or the skin changes, come straight back. Don't wait on the letter.",
  "[SEG0044] person_1 (PATIENT): Fine. Are we finished. I need to get to school."
 ],
